<title>USA: Allegiance Corp Q4 oper net up.</title>
<headline>Allegiance Corp Q4 oper net up.</headline>
<dateline>MCGAW PARK, Ill. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $0.32		    $0.21</p>
<p> Oper net		   17,300		   11,600</p>
<p> Revs		    1,091,900		1,178,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   54,900		   54,900</p>
<p>			12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		    $1.15		    $1.16</p>
<p> Oper net		   63,100		   63,900</p>
<p> Revs		    4,386,700		4,571,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   54,900		   54,900</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 Q4 and both 12-mos period are pro forma and include adjustments to historical financial data. Company was spun off from Baxter International Inc September 1996.</p>
<p>1996 Q4 and 12-mos net and shr exclude $645.5 million one-time charge on reported losses of $595.5 million for Q4 and $549.7 million for 1996. Largest charge was $550 million non-cash write-down of goodwill on change in accounting method. Additional one-time charge in Q4 was $95.5 million on facility consolidation and other asset write-downs. After charges, 1996 Q4 shr loss was $10.85.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
